# DS wrapper authoring

Applies to Mantine wrappers under `components/DesignSystem/`. **Does not apply** to `ComplexComponents/` (`PageContentHeader`, `DataTable`, …). Those are AppDirect compositions: they compose DS primitives and must not use the `extends MantineX` recipe.

## When a Mantine component has no DS wrapper

Create one, typed as `DS[Name]Props extends Mantine[Name]Props`, `forwardRef`, export through the category index and `components/DesignSystem/index.ts`.

```tsx
import React, { forwardRef } from 'react';
import { [MantineComponent] as Mantine[Component], [MantineComponent]Props as Mantine[Component]Props } from '@mantine/core';

export interface DS[Component]Props extends Mantine[Component]Props {}

export const [Component] = forwardRef<HTML[Element]Element, DS[Component]Props>(
  ({ ...props }, ref) => <Mantine[Component] ref={ref} {...props} />
);
[Component].displayName = '[Component]';
```

Raw `@mantine/core` imports are allowed **inside these wrapper files**. App and prototype pages still import from `@/components/DesignSystem`.

Shared enums live in `components/DesignSystem/types.ts` and must match the wrapper that imports them. Wrapper TSX is the implementation source of truth.

Do not put Code Connect serializer rules here — use `.cursor/rules/figma-code-connect.mdc` on `*.figma.tsx`.
